# ============================================================
# Multi-tenant ISOLATION test suite — opt-in env.
# Copy this file to `.env.test` and fill in the values to enable
# `src/lib/orgs/isolation.test.ts`.
#
# Without these vars, the suite is skipped (vitest displays it in
# gray), so `npm test` and the CI pipeline keep passing.
#
# ⚠️ Use a SEPARATE Supabase project for tests — never point this at
# the dev or production project. The suite creates and destroys real
# users, orgs and tenant rows.
# ============================================================

# Project URL — Settings → API
TEST_SUPABASE_URL=https://<test-project-ref>.supabase.co

# `anon` / public key
TEST_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=...

# `service_role` (secret) — bypasses RLS, used to provision and clean
# up. NEVER commit a real value.
TEST_SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=...

# ============================================================
# Setup steps
# ============================================================
# 1. supabase.com → Create new project (free tier is fine).
# 2. SQL Editor → New query → paste `supabase/apply_all_migrations.sql`
#    (the 18 migrations) → Run.
# 3. Copy this file to `.env.test`, fill in the 3 vars above.
# 4. Load the env and run the tests:
#      set -a; source .env.test; set +a; npm test
#    (PowerShell:
#      Get-Content .env.test | ForEach-Object {
#        if ($_ -match '^([A-Z_]+)=(.*)$') {
#          [Environment]::SetEnvironmentVariable($Matches[1], $Matches[2], 'Process')
#        }
#      }
#      npm test)
# 5. The "multi-tenant isolation" describe block now runs (~30 s
#    against the test project). All cases must be green before
#    shipping to the 1st paying customer.
#
# To enable in CI (GitHub Actions):
#   - Repo Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions → New secret
#     for each of the 3 vars.
#   - Reference them in the `env:` block of `.github/workflows/ci.yml`.
# ============================================================
